IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Australian Charities and Not-for-profits Commission Act 2012 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- must my foundation register, what
-- does registration give it, and how can it be lost: the object of Part 2-1 (s 20-5); entitlement to registration as a charity
-- and as a subtype (s 25-5); the process (ss 30-10, 30-15, 30-20, 30-25, 30-30, 30-35); revocation and show cause (ss 35-5,
-- 35-10, 35-15, 35-20); the Register (ss 40-5(1)(a), (c), 40-10(1), (2), (3)); objections (ss 160-5, 160-10).
--
-- SEAT: the founder of a charity and director of its trustee company -- a responsible person of the registered entity (in
-- Daniel's life, the Rossi Foundation, a private ancillary fund). "Must my foundation register, what does registration give it,
-- and what can be done to it?" The Commissioner's beliefs, satisfactions and choices are asked as facts or answered
-- conditionally; the Act's duties fall on the registered entity, so they are asked as "my foundation".
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 11, compilation date 5 December 2025 (includes amendments up to Act No. 72, 2025), register id
-- C2025C00665, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2012A00168.txt. The Australian Charities and Not-for-profits
-- Commission Regulations 2022 (governance standards, external conduct standards) are NOT DEPOSITED: compliance with the standards
-- is an INPUT. "Charity" (Charities Act 2013) and "not-for-profit entity" are borrowed terms (this Act does not define them),
-- asked as facts.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Cy pres (s 25-5(6)); the Commissioner's requirement for further information itself (s 30-15(1)); the date of effect
-- the Commissioner chooses (s 30-30 -- an input); the s 35-10(2) matters the Commissioner weighs (the decision to revoke is asked
-- as a fact); former registered entities on the Register (s 40-5(1)(b)); the Register's other contents (s 40-5(1)(d) to (g));
-- objection decisions and review by the ART and the courts (ss 160-15 to 170-30); the external conduct standards (Division 50).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Australian Charities and Not-for-profits Commission Act 2012 -- registration`

§§ `s 20-5 -- what registration gives my foundation`

-- s 20-5(2): "Such registration is a prerequisite for an entity to access certain Commonwealth tax concessions. The object of this
-- Part is to ensure that these tax concessions are available only to entities that are governed and regulated in accordance with
-- this Act." (3): "Registration under this Act may also be a prerequisite for other exemptions, benefits and concessions provided
-- under other Australian laws." s 30-10(1): "An entity MAY apply to the Commissioner for registration." Nothing in this Act obliges
-- an entity to register: the obligation, if any, is in the law granting the concession (for a private ancillary fund's deductible
-- gift recipient status, the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 -- not read here). s 30-30: "The registration has effect from a date
-- specified by the Commissioner." s 35-10(3): a revocation takes effect from the day it specifies.
-- "registered entity" (s 300-5): "an entity that is registered under this Act".
@export Is my foundation registered on a given day, and so meets the prerequisite for tax concessions that require registration (ss 20-5(2), 30-30, 35-10(3))?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask about, ISO 8601
      `it has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has registered your foundation
      `the date of effect` IS A DATE @desc The date of effect the Commissioner specified for the registration (s 30-30)
      `it has been revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the registration has been revoked
      `the day the revocation takes effect` IS A DATE @desc The day the revocation specifies (ignored if not revoked)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my foundation registered on the day` IF
        `it has been registered`
    AND `the date of effect` AT MOST `the day`
    AND (NOT (`it has been revoked` AND `the day the revocation takes effect` AT MOST `the day`))

§§ `s 25-5 -- is my foundation entitled to registration`

-- s 25-5(1): "An entity is entitled to registration as a type of entity if: (a) it meets the conditions in subsection (3); and (b)
-- it meets the description of that type of entity in column 1 of the table in subsection (5); and (c) if the entity has previously
-- been a registered entity, but its registration as a type of entity has been revoked--the Commissioner is satisfied that the
-- matters which led to the revocation have been dealt with". (3): "(a) the entity is a not-for-profit entity; (b) the entity is in
-- compliance with the governance standards and external conduct standards (see Part 3-1); (c) the entity has an ABN; (d) the entity
-- is not covered by a decision in writing made by an Australian government agency ... that provides for entities to be
-- characterised on the basis of them engaging in, or supporting, terrorist or other criminal activities." Column 1 of the table
-- has one type: "Charity" ("For the definition of charity, see the Charities Act 2013").
DECLARE `My foundation` HAS
    `it is a not-for-profit entity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a charity under the Charities Act 2013` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it complies with the governance standards` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it complies with the external conduct standards` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it has an ABN` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is listed by a written decision as engaging in or supporting terrorist or criminal activity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `its registration was revoked before` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner is satisfied the matters behind the revocation are dealt with` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `f` IS A `My foundation` @desc Your foundation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it meets the s 25-5(3) conditions` IF
        `f`'s `it is a not-for-profit entity`
    AND `f`'s `it complies with the governance standards`
    AND `f`'s `it complies with the external conduct standards`
    AND `f`'s `it has an ABN`
    AND (NOT `f`'s `it is listed by a written decision as engaging in or supporting terrorist or criminal activity`)

@export Is my foundation entitled to registration as a charity (s 25-5(1), (3), (5) column 1)?
GIVEN `the foundation` IS A `My foundation` @desc What your foundation is and whether it meets the conditions; the governance and external conduct standards are in the Regulations, not deposited, so compliance is asked as a fact
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my foundation entitled to registration as a charity` IF
        `it meets the s 25-5(3) conditions` `the foundation`
    AND `the foundation`'s `it is a charity under the Charities Act 2013`
    AND (    (NOT `the foundation`'s `its registration was revoked before`)
          OR `the foundation`'s `the Commissioner is satisfied the matters behind the revocation are dealt with`)

-- s 25-5(5), column 2: the subtypes of a charity, items 1 to 12 by paragraph (a) to (l) of the definition of "charitable purpose"
-- in s 12(1) of the Charities Act 2013, item 13 a health promotion charity, item 14 a public benevolent institution. (4): "an
-- entity may be entitled to registration as more than one subtype". The table is the enumeration.
DECLARE `Subtype of charity` IS ONE OF
    `advancing health`
    `advancing education`
    `advancing social or public welfare`
    `advancing religion`
    `advancing culture`
    `promoting reconciliation, mutual respect and tolerance`
    `promoting or protecting human rights`
    `advancing the security or safety of Australia or the Australian public`
    `preventing or relieving the suffering of animals`
    `advancing the natural environment`
    `other purposes beneficial to the general public`
    `advancing public debate`
    `promoting the prevention or control of diseases in human beings`
    `public benevolent institution`

-- s 25-5(2): entitled to registration as a subtype if "(a) it meets the conditions in subsection (3); and (b) it meets the
-- description of that subtype ... in column 2 ...; and (c) it is entitled to registration as the type of entity that corresponds to
-- that subtype ...; and (d) it is registered as that type of entity."
@export Is my foundation entitled to registration as a subtype of charity (s 25-5(2), (5) column 2)?
GIVEN `the foundation` IS A `My foundation` @desc What your foundation is and whether it meets the conditions
      `the subtype` IS A `Subtype of charity` @desc The subtype applied for (column 2 of the table in s 25-5(5))
      `it meets the description of the subtype` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it has the purpose, or is the institution, the subtype describes
      `it is registered as a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is already registered as a charity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my foundation entitled to registration as the subtype` IF
        `it meets the s 25-5(3) conditions` `the foundation`
    AND `it meets the description of the subtype`
    AND `Is my foundation entitled to registration as a charity` `the foundation`
    AND `it is registered as a charity`

§§ `ss 30-15, 30-20 -- must the Commissioner register my foundation, and how long may it wait`

-- s 30-20: "The Commissioner must register the applicant if: (a) the application is in the approved form; and (b) if the
-- Commissioner has required the applicant under subsection 30-15(1) to give information or a document--the applicant has given the
-- Commissioner that information or document; and (c) the applicant is entitled to registration under Division 25." s 30-25: the
-- Commissioner "must give the applicant written notice" of registration or refusal.
@export Must the Commissioner register my foundation as a charity (s 30-20)?
GIVEN `the foundation` IS A `My foundation` @desc What your foundation is and whether it meets the conditions
      `the application is in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application was made in the approved form (s 30-10(2))
      `the Commissioner required more information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner required information or a document under s 30-15(1)
      `I gave what was required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the foundation gave everything the Commissioner required
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Commissioner register my foundation` IF
        `the application is in the approved form`
    AND ((NOT `the Commissioner required more information`) OR `I gave what was required`)
    AND `Is my foundation entitled to registration as a charity` `the foundation`

-- s 30-15(2): "After the time worked out under subsection (3), the applicant may give the Commissioner, in the approved form,
-- written notice that the applicant wishes to treat the application as having been refused" if not yet told the outcome. (3):
-- "The time is the end of the 60th day after the application was made. However, if before that time the Commissioner requires the
-- applicant under subsection (1) to give information or a document, the time is the later of ...: (a) the end of the 28th day after
-- the last day on which the applicant gives the Commissioner information or a document that the Commissioner has required ...; (b)
-- the end of the 60th day after the application was made." (4): the notice operates as a refusal on the day it is given, so the
-- applicant may object (s 30-35).
@export On what day does the Commissioner's time to decide my foundation's application end, after which it may treat the application as refused (s 30-15(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the day I applied` IS A DATE @desc The day the application was made, ISO 8601
      `the Commissioner required information in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before the end of the 60th day, the Commissioner required information or a document
      `the last day I gave required information` IS A DATE @desc The last day the foundation gave required information (ignored if none was required)
GIVETH A DATE
`When does the Commissioner's time to decide end` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner required information in time` AND `info` GREATER THAN `sixty`
    THEN `info` ELSE `sixty`
    WHERE
        `sixty` MEANS `the day I applied` PLUS 60
        `info` MEANS `the last day I gave required information` PLUS 28

§§ `s 35-10 -- can my foundation's registration be revoked`

-- s 35-10(1): "The Commissioner may revoke the registration of a registered entity if the Commissioner reasonably believes that any
-- of the following conditions are met: (a) at any time after the date of effect of the registration, the entity is or was not
-- entitled to registration; (b) the registered entity provided, in connection with its application for registration, information
-- that was false or misleading in a material particular; (c) at any time after the date of effect of the registration: (i) the
-- registered entity has contravened a provision of this Act, or it is more likely than not that [it] will ...; or (ii) the
-- registered entity has not complied with a governance standard or external conduct standard, or it is more likely than not that
-- [it] will not comply ...; (d) the registered entity has: (i) a trustee in bankruptcy; or (ii) a liquidator; or (iii) a person
-- appointed ... to manage [its] affairs ... because it is unable to pay all its debts ...; (e) the registered entity has made a
-- request ... in the approved form". Every limb is something "the Commissioner reasonably believes": asked as such.
-- s 35-5(2): revoking the type revokes every subtype.
DECLARE `What the Commissioner reasonably believes` HAS
    `my foundation is or was not entitled to registration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my foundation gave false or misleading information in its application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my foundation contravened, or will likely contravene, the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my foundation did not, or will likely not, comply with a governance or external conduct standard` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my foundation has a trustee in bankruptcy, liquidator or insolvency manager` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my foundation asked in the approved form for revocation` IS A BOOLEAN

@export May the Commissioner revoke my foundation's registration (s 35-10(1))?
GIVEN `belief` IS A `What the Commissioner reasonably believes` @desc Which of the grounds the Commissioner reasonably believes are met
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commissioner revoke my foundation's registration` IF
        `belief`'s `my foundation is or was not entitled to registration`
    OR  `belief`'s `my foundation gave false or misleading information in its application`
    OR  `belief`'s `my foundation contravened, or will likely contravene, the Act`
    OR  `belief`'s `my foundation did not, or will likely not, comply with a governance or external conduct standard`
    OR  `belief`'s `my foundation has a trustee in bankruptcy, liquidator or insolvency manager`
    OR  `belief`'s `my foundation asked in the approved form for revocation`

-- s 35-10(3): "The specified day must be: (a) if the reason for the revocation is that the entity is not entitled to registration:
-- (i) the day on which the entity first ceased to be entitled; or (ii) a later day; or (b) if the reason ... is that the entity
-- provided ... information that was false or misleading in a material particular: (i) the day on which the registration took effect;
-- or (ii) a later day; or (c) otherwise: (i) the day on which the revocation is made; or (ii) a later day."
DECLARE `Why the registration is revoked` IS ONE OF
    `it is not entitled to registration`
    `it gave false or misleading information in its application`
    `another reason`

@export What is the earliest day from which my foundation's registration can be taken to be revoked (s 35-10(3))?
GIVEN `the reason` IS A `Why the registration is revoked` @desc The reason for the revocation
      `the day it first ceased to be entitled` IS A DATE @desc The day it first ceased to be entitled to registration, ISO 8601
      `the day its registration took effect` IS A DATE @desc The date of effect of the registration, ISO 8601
      `the day the revocation is made` IS A DATE @desc The day the Commissioner makes the revocation, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`From when can the revocation take effect at the earliest` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reason`
    WHEN `it is not entitled to registration` THEN `the day it first ceased to be entitled`
    WHEN `it gave false or misleading information in its application` THEN `the day its registration took effect`
    OTHERWISE `the day the revocation is made`

-- s 35-10(4): "The Commissioner must give the entity written notice within 14 days if the Commissioner revokes its registration."
@export By when must my foundation be given written notice that its registration has been revoked (s 35-10(4))?
GIVEN `the day the revocation is made` IS A DATE @desc The day the Commissioner revokes the registration, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my foundation be told of the revocation` MEANS
    `the day the revocation is made` PLUS 14

§§ `s 35-15 -- show cause`

-- s 35-15(1): "Before revoking the registration, the Commissioner must give a written notice (a show cause notice) to the registered
-- entity." (2)(b): it must "invite the registered entity to give the Commissioner, within 28 days after the day the notice is given,
-- a written statement showing cause". (3): not if the Commissioner "believes, on reasonable grounds and taking into account the
-- matters mentioned in subsection 35-10(2), that it would be appropriate ... to revoke the registration without giving a show cause
-- notice". The same 28 days apply before a responsible entity is suspended or removed (ss 100-10(5), 100-15(4)).
@export Must my foundation be given a show cause notice before its registration is revoked (s 35-15(1), (3))?
GIVEN `the Commissioner believes it appropriate to act without one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner believes, on reasonable grounds and having regard to s 35-10(2), that revoking without a show cause notice is appropriate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my foundation be given a show cause notice` IF
    NOT `the Commissioner believes it appropriate to act without one`

@export By when may my foundation give its written statement showing cause (ss 35-15(2)(b), 100-10(5)(b), 100-15(4)(b))?
GIVEN `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE @desc The day the show cause notice is given, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`By when may my foundation show cause` MEANS
    `the day the notice is given` PLUS 28

§§ `ss 40-5, 40-10 -- what the Register shows about me`

-- s 40-5(1): the Register includes "(c) the following details in respect of each responsible entity of each registered entity: (i)
-- the name of each responsible entity; (ii) the position held by the responsible entity in relation to the registered entity". (4):
-- "The Register is to be made available for public inspection on the internet." s 40-10(1): regulations may provide that the
-- Commissioner "must not include information on the Register, or must remove information" (not deposited -- asked as a fact). (2):
-- the Commissioner "may decline to include information ... or may remove information" if the Commissioner considers it commercially
-- sensitive and potentially detrimental, inaccurate or misleading, offensive, or endangering public safety (among others); (3): the
-- public interest may outweigh. The Commissioner's view is asked as a fact.
@export Will my name and position as a responsible person of my foundation be published on the Register (ss 40-5(1)(c), 40-10)?
GIVEN `I am a responsible entity of a registered entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a responsible entity (s 205-30) of an entity that is registered
      `a regulation forbids including it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a regulation under s 40-10(1) forbids it or requires its removal (the Regulations are not deposited)
      `the Commissioner has decided to withhold or remove it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has decided under s 40-10(2), the public interest not outweighing, to leave it off or take it off
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my name be on the Register` IF
        `I am a responsible entity of a registered entity`
    AND (NOT `a regulation forbids including it`)
    AND (NOT `the Commissioner has decided to withhold or remove it`)

§§ `ss 160-5, 160-10 -- objecting`

-- An entity "dissatisfied" may object "in the manner set out in Part 7-2": against a refusal to register (s 30-35), a revocation or a
-- decision not to revoke (s 35-20); a responsible entity against its suspension or removal (ss 100-10(10), 100-15(7)). s 160-5:
-- "(a) make it in the approved form; and (b) lodge it with the Commissioner within the review period ...; and (c) state in it, fully
-- and in detail, the grounds". s 160-10(1): "within the period of 60 days (the review period) after notice of the administrative
-- decision has been served on the entity." (2)-(6): a late objection may be lodged with a written request; if the Commissioner
-- agrees, "the objection is treated as having been lodged within the review period".
@export By when must the objection be lodged (s 160-10(1))?
GIVEN `the day the notice was served` IS A DATE @desc The day notice of the decision was served, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I object` MEANS
    `the day the notice was served` PLUS 60

@export Is the objection treated as lodged within the review period (s 160-10)?
GIVEN `the day the notice was served` IS A DATE @desc The day notice of the decision was served, ISO 8601
      `the day it was lodged` IS A DATE @desc The day the objection was lodged, ISO 8601
      `a written request for late lodgement went with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a written request, with full reasons for the lateness, was lodged with it
      `the Commissioner agreed to the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner agreed to the request (s 160-10(4))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the objection in time` IF
        `the day it was lodged` AT MOST `By when must I object` `the day the notice was served`
    OR  (`a written request for late lodgement went with it` AND `the Commissioner agreed to the request`)
